  "privacySection1Title": "1. Information We Collect",
  "privacySection1Body": "CropGuard AI collects: account email and display name (if signed in), crop images processed on-device, coarsened location coordinates (~1.1 km grid) to deliver microclimate weather and regional outbreak alerts without exposing exact farm boundaries, and aggregate usage telemetry. We do not sell your personal data.",
  "privacySection2Title": "2. How We Use Your Data",
  "privacySection2Body": "Your data is used to provide on-device disease diagnosis, localized spray and weather advisories, community outbreak mapping, and expert consultation. Scan images and exact farm locations are never shared publicly.",
  "privacySection3Title": "3. Data Storage & Retention",
  "privacySection3Body": "Scan records are stored locally on your device via SQLite. Map tiles and geocoding names are cached on device disk to enable offline functionality. Cloud sync is optional and gated behind authentication. You can delete your local scan history in Settings or request complete account deletion at any time.",
  "privacySection4Title": "4. Third-Party Services",
  "privacySection4Body": "We use Supabase for secure authentication and optional sync, OpenStreetMap and Nominatim for map tiles and place names, Open-Meteo for localized weather, and Ghana NLP for local language synthesis. We do not share data with any other third parties.",
  "privacySection5Title": "5. Contact",
  "privacySection5Body": "For privacy enquiries or data deletion requests, contact privacy@cropguardai.com.",
  "termsSection1Title": "1. Acceptance of Terms",
  "termsSection1Body": "By using CropGuard AI, you agree to these Terms of Service. If you disagree with any part, please do not use the application.",
  "termsSection2Title": "2. Medical / Agronomical Disclaimer",
  "termsSection2Body": "CropGuard AI provides guidance based on AI image analysis. Results are not a substitute for expert agronomical advice. Always consult a qualified agronomist before applying treatments, especially chemical pesticides.",
  "termsSection3Title": "3. User Responsibilities",
  "termsSection3Body": "You are responsible for the accuracy of information you provide, appropriate use of treatment recommendations, and compliance with local agricultural regulations.",
